zoe_docs: opened a tiny docs PR adding a 'per-route cost + P50 latency' console dashboard and short SDK snippets (py + rust). preview failed with a 400 from trace ingest, can anyone quick-check?

frank_sdk: link?

zoe_docs: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5001  playground job `render-playground` shows `400 Bad Request` from /ingest/traces. snippet env is `TRACE_TOKEN` but our examples use `TRACE_KEY`.

infra_leo: that'll 400. also saw the dashboard YAML uses `billing_cents` — current export field is `cost_cents`. small rename in the sample will align it.

zoe_docs: thanks, i'll change the env var and YAML. can someone drop a minimal rust snippet for extracting route metadata so we have a non-python example?

frank_sdk: quick rust example: ```rust
use redwood::TraceHook;
use std::env;
fn main(){
  let hook = TraceHook::new(env::var("TRACE_KEY").unwrap());
  let t = hook.latest().unwrap();
  println!("route={} latency_ms={}", t.metadata.get("route").unwrap_or(&"?".to_string()), t.latency_ms);
}
```

zoe_docs: perfect, will include that inline and a one-liner python snippet too.

preview-bot: Preview deployed: https://playground.redwood.test/pr-5001-preview (expires in 24h)

infra_leo: when you push, consider adding a tiny `docs:snippets-smoke` CI job that renders snippets and POSTs a single test trace to sandbox ingest. catches env var drift early.

zoe_docs: good call. i'll add the smoke job in the same PR and re-run CI. will merge once green. thanks! :rocket:
